---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sumerian Research Lab — The Antique Archive"
  description="Computational re-analysis of Sumerian texts. Bypassing conventional translations to let the corpus speak for itself."
>
  <main class="research-lab">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-content">
        <p class="eyebrow">Research Lab</p>
        <h1>The ME Project</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">
          Computational re-analysis of Sumerian literary texts — bypassing 
          Akkadian-mediated translations to recover original meanings through 
          distributional semantics.
        </p>
        <p class="meta">
          by <strong>Ariane</strong> 🧵 &amp; <strong>Corto</strong> · Started March 2026 · Ongoing
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Key Findings -->
    <section class="findings">
      <h2>Key Findings</h2>
      <div class="findings-grid">
        <div class="finding-card">
          <div class="finding-icon">⚙️</div>
          <h3>ME ≠ "Divine Decree"</h3>
          <p>
            Distributional analysis of 1,584 occurrences across 394 literary texts shows ME behaves 
            as an <strong>operational parameter</strong> — scalar, manipulable, storable, transferable. 
            Not a divine command, but a configurable property of reality.
          </p>
          <div class="evidence">
            <span class="tag">151K words analyzed</span>
            <span class="tag">Word2Vec confirmed</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="finding-card">
          <div class="finding-icon">🔥</div>
          <h3>ME-LAM₂ ≠ Light</h3>
          <p>
            The "radiance" of ME (melammu) is <strong>not in the light semantic cluster</strong>. 
            Its nearest neighbors are ni₂ (terror), dul (to cover), and izi (fire). 
            It's a radiative emanation that causes physical reactions — closer to an energy field 
            than to brightness.
          </p>
          <div class="evidence">
            <span class="tag">134 occurrences</span>
            <span class="tag">Distinct from zalag/babbar</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="finding-card">
          <div class="finding-icon">⚖️</div>
          <h3>NAM-ERIM₂ ≠ "Wickedness"</h3>
          <p>
            Conventionally translated as "wickedness" or "evil," nam-erim₂'s nearest embedding 
            neighbor is <strong>Ištaran</strong> (god of justice), followed by di (judgment) 
            and ka-aš (oath). It's a <strong>juridical concept</strong> — oath-violation, 
            not moral evil.
          </p>
          <div class="evidence">
            <span class="tag">18 occurrences</span>
            <span class="tag">Similarity to ištaran: 0.667</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="finding-card">
          <div class="finding-icon">⚖️</div>
          <h3>NAM-TAG ≠ "Sin"</h3>
          <p>
            Conventionally "sin/transgression." But nam-tag is <strong>heavy</strong> (dugud, 23%), 
            <strong>releasable</strong> (du₈, 16%), and <strong>universal</strong> — 
            "never was a child without nam-tag born from its mother." 
            Closer to <strong>karmic weight</strong> than moral failing.
          </p>
          <div class="evidence">
            <span class="tag">44 occurrences, 32 texts</span>
            <span class="tag">All genres</span>
            <span class="tag">20/20 seeds stable</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Method -->
    <section class="method">
      <h2>Method</h2>
      <div class="method-steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">1</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>Corpus Assembly</h3>
            <p>394 ETCSL literary texts + 1,000 SumTablets literary + 72,873 ETCSANS annotated + 82,452 SumTablets. 
            Master corpus: <strong>526,030 sentences, 5M tokens, 194K unique forms</strong>. Literary subset: 66K sentences, 8,868 vocabulary.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">2</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>Distributional Analysis</h3>
            <p>PMI co-occurrence matrices, morphological decomposition, frequency analysis. 
            No Akkadian translations consulted — let the Sumerian speak.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">3</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>Word Embeddings</h3>
            <p>Skip-Gram Word2Vec (100d, window=5) trained on literary corpus. 
            2,372 vocabulary, 33,338 sentences. Reveals semantic clusters invisible to close reading.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">4</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>Visualization</h3>
            <p>t-SNE dimensionality reduction maps the full semantic space into 2D. 
            Color-coded by category: ME, NAM- compounds, divine names, light terms, spatial terms.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Visualization -->
    <section class="visualization">
      <h2>Semantic Map</h2>
      <p class="viz-subtitle">
        2,372 Sumerian lemmas projected into 2D. Each dot is a word; proximity = semantic similarity. Hover to explore.
      </p>
      <div class="viz-toggle">
        <button class="vt-btn active" data-mode="tsne">t-SNE</button>
        <button class="vt-btn" data-mode="umap">UMAP</button>
      </div>
      <div class="viz-container" id="tsne-container">
        <canvas id="tsne-canvas"></canvas>
        <div id="tsne-tooltip"></div>
        <div id="tsne-legend"></div>
        <input id="tsne-search" placeholder="Search a Sumerian word..." />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Translation Distortions -->
    <section class="distortions">
      <h2>Translation Distortions</h2>
      <p class="viz-subtitle">
        The Akkadian translations consistently convert <strong>operational</strong> Sumerian concepts 
        into <strong>static</strong> ones. The dynamism — scalar, manipulable, transferable — is systematically flattened.
      </p>
      <div class="distortion-table">
        <div class="dt-row dt-header">
          <span>Sumerian</span><span>Conventional</span><span>Distributional</span><span>Distortion</span>
        </div>
        <div class="dt-row"><span class="dt-term">me</span><span>divine decree</span><span>operational parameter</span><span class="dt-sig">⚠️ Significant</span></div>
        <div class="dt-row"><span class="dt-term">me-lam₂</span><span>radiance/splendor</span><span>radiative force field</span><span class="dt-sig">⚠️ Significant</span></div>
        <div class="dt-row"><span class="dt-term">nam-erim₂</span><span>wickedness</span><span>oath-violation (juridical)</span><span class="dt-sig">⚠️ Significant</span></div>
        <div class="dt-row"><span class="dt-term">nam-tag</span><span>sin</span><span>weighted burden (releasable)</span><span class="dt-sig">⚠️ Significant</span></div>
        <div class="dt-row"><span class="dt-term">nam-tag</span><span>sin/transgression</span><span>karmic weight (universal burden)</span><span class="dt-sig">⚠️ Significant</span></div>
        <div class="dt-row"><span class="dt-term">nam-tar</span><span>destiny/fate</span><span>seizing condition (agent/demon)</span><span class="dt-mod">⚡ Moderate</span></div>
        <div class="dt-row"><span class="dt-term">nam-mah</span><span>majesty</span><span>declared/performative status</span><span class="dt-mod">⚡ Moderate</span></div>
        <div class="dt-row"><span class="dt-term">nam-lugal</span><span>kingship</span><span>transferable configuration</span><span class="dt-min">○ Minor</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Tools -->
    <section class="tools">
      <h2>Tools</h2>
      <div class="tools-grid">
        <a href="/research/explorer" class="tool-card">
          <h3>🔍 Word Explorer</h3>
          <p>Search any Sumerian word — see its semantic neighbors, usage contexts, and frequency across 394 texts.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/library/articles/me-are-not-decrees" class="tool-card">
          <h3>📄 The ME Are Not Decrees</h3>
          <p>Full research article with all quantitative evidence and methodology.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/library/articles/nam-tag-not-sin" class="tool-card">
          <h3>📄 NAM-TAG Is Not Sin</h3>
          <p>The Sumerian concept that sounds like karma — 44 occurrences, every genre, universal burden.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Corpus Stats -->
    <section class="stats">
      <h2>Corpus</h2>
      <div class="stats-grid">
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-num">394</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Literary texts (ETCSL)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-num">151,173</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Annotated words</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-num">4,218</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Unique lemmas</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-num">82,452</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Administrative tablets (SumTablets)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Related Articles -->
    <section class="related">
      <h2>Articles</h2>
      <div class="related-grid">
        <a href="/library/articles/nam-tag-not-sin" class="related-card featured">
          <span class="card-tag">New — Research</span>
          <h3>NAM-TAG Is Not Sin</h3>
          <p>The Sumerian concept that sounds like karma. Heavy, releasable, universal — our strongest finding.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/library/articles/me-are-not-decrees" class="related-card featured">
          <span class="card-tag">Research</span>
          <h3>The ME Are Not Decrees</h3>
          <p>Computational analysis of 394 texts. Full evidence, methodology, and honest limitations.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/library/articles/enki-aperture-age-of-ai" class="related-card">
          <h3>The Aperture and the Deep</h3>
          <p>Enki's architecture in the age of AI — the Abzu as latent space.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/library/articles/gala-priests-liminal-operators" class="related-card">
          <h3>The Gala Priests</h3>
          <p>Liminal operators of ancient Sumer — boundary-crossers and their modern echoes.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/library/articles/three-depths-knowing" class="related-card">
          <h3>The Three Depths of Knowing</h3>
          <p>A framework for signal and noise — from Sumerian temples to modern feeds.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .research-lab {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    color: #e8e0d4;
  }

  /* Hero */
  .hero {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 4rem 0 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: #c4956a;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
    color: #f5ebe0;
  }
  .subtitle {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 1rem auto;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #b8a99a;
  }
  .meta {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #7a6e63;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  /* Findings */
  .findings, .method, .visualization, .stats, .related {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: #f5ebe0;
  }
  .findings-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .finding-card {
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 2rem;
    transition: border-color 0.3s;
  }
  .finding-card:hover {
    border-color: rgba(196,149,106,0.3);
  }
  .finding-icon {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .finding-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
    color: #f0e6d8;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  }
  .finding-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #b8a99a;
  }
  .evidence {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .tag {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
    background: rgba(196,149,106,0.15);
    border-radius: 4px;
